course: dictionary
lesson: 2372
title: A word for a storm cloud
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names for things in the sky. A cumulonimbus is a kind of cloud, and the clues in the sentences tell you what it is. «Cumulonimbus clouds are tall storm clouds that bring heavy rain, thunder and hail.» The words storm, rain, thunder and hail tell you this cloud belongs to bad weather.
explain: «A thunderstorm grows when warm, damp air rises very fast and cools, building a tall, dark tower of cloud called a cumulonimbus.» The word called tells you that cumulonimbus is the name for that tall, dark tower of cloud.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Could you say «a tall storm cloud» instead of cumulonimbus and still make sense? Yes, so your meaning fits. Clouds are named by their shape and height: «cumulus are white puffy heaps of fair weather; stratus are flat grey sheets that may bring drizzle; cirrus are thin wisps of ice high up.»
fact: A cumulonimbus is a very tall, heavy, dark cloud.
fact: It brings thunderstorms, heavy rain, hail or lightning.
fact: It is the biggest kind of cloud, and its flat top can be shaped like an anvil.
fact: The name comes from Latin: cumulus means heap, and nimbus means rain cloud.
fact: When you see thunder clouds, get indoors and away from tall trees and water.
exercise: «Cumulonimbus clouds are tall storm clouds that bring heavy rain, thunder and hail.» What is a cumulonimbus? | A small white puff on a sunny day | A flat grey sheet that brings drizzle | *A tall, heavy, dark cloud that can bring storms | A thin wisp of ice high in the sky
exercise: A cumulonimbus can have a flat top. What is that top shaped like? | A bicycle wheel | A football | *An anvil | A square box
exercise: Thunder clouds are coming. What is the safest thing to do? | Go swimming in the lake | Stand under a tall tree | Hold an umbrella and wait outside | *Get indoors and stay away from tall trees and water
test: In the name cumulonimbus, what does the Latin word nimbus mean? | Thunder | *A rain cloud | Hail | A heap
test: Which cloud is described as thin wisps of ice high up? | Cumulonimbus | Stratus | Cumulus | *Cirrus
exam: Which of these best describes a cumulonimbus? | A flat grey sheet of drizzle | A cloud with thin wisps of ice that never rains | A small white puff on a sunny day | *A tall, dark storm cloud that brings heavy rain and thunder
